From 85d801a22e78ad0cd63c873a02df1c9432b1abc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anthonybartczak <49080651+anthonybartczak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:11:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Say whether the events channel answered its handshake

A session opened a few seconds after another one ended, or after the
pedal powered up, can get no reply to its HELLO on the events channel.
Requests work, but no notification arrives for the whole session. Seen
on an HX Effects (firmware 3.80): every open 0 to 4 s after a session
ended was like that, and none 15 s or more after. The replay fixture
records such a session: 42 stale events frames, then the events HELLO
unanswered and no events frame afterwards.

- `route` notes each channel's HELLO reply, and
  `Session::events_answered` reports the events channel's. The
  handshake bytes are unchanged and nothing is retried.
- The fake pedal answers handshakes, and `deaf_events` makes it leave
  the events one unanswered.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
